  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.outgoing_edges.fn` only says that criterion code uses `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.outgoing_edges` for this operation. The only structural content is the signature in that cited requirement. The cited requirement is context, not a separate subject.\n\nThe implementation root is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2/fn[outgoing_edges]`. Its signature matches the cited one:\n- It takes `&self`, `node: &NodeId<D>` and `label: D::EdgeLabel`.\n- It returns `Result<Snapshot<Vec<NodeId<D>>>, D::Error>`.\n- It has the bound `D::EdgeLabel: PartialEq`.\n\nIt gets the targets and fingerprint from `prepare_edges`, records the observation with `observe_edges`, and returns the snapshot.\n\nThe operation is also the one that the context's own helper uses: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[successors]` calls `self.outgoing_edges(&self.node, label.clone())`. The test-agent tool `execute` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` calls it too.\n\nI found no structural gap and no acknowledgments. The requirement states no runtime behavior beyond the cited requirement, so I did not assess any here.",
